off may affect crew cooperation. Not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. So reliability good, stress resilience good, but communication issue (nasty remarks) and memory issue (numbers) could affect attention and professional communication.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So decision quality good, stress resilience good, but communication and adaptability issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. So reliability, attention, problem solving good, but hot temper may affect crew cooperation, know-it-all may affect teamwork.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate has strongest overall? Let's weigh.\n\nCandidate B: strong on reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). But nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation and professional communication. Memory for numbers could affect attention.\n\nCandidate C: strong decision speed, calm, technical understanding. But egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education (adaptability). Could be problematic.\n\nCandidate D: strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, handles unexpected events. But hot temper and know-it-all attitude could affect crew cooperation and communication.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. But show-off, not open to new ideas. Could affect crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate D: strong across many criteria, only hot temper and know-it-all. But hot temper could be serious under pressure. Candidate B's nasty remarks also serious. Candidate C's egocentric also serious. Candidate A's show-off maybe less severe? Not open to new ideas could affect adaptability.\n\nWe might start by recommending Candidate D, but note concerns. Or we could ask another panel member for more info on hot temper severity. But we need to make a public contribution now. We can give initial recommendation for Candidate D, citing strengths and concerns, and ask others for more info on crew cooperation.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON vote.\n\nLet's produce public message: \"I propose Candidate D as the leading candidate because...\" and include facts.\n\nProceed."}
